week 6
-- llm baseline evaluation --

-- ollama runs the llama3.2 model locally to answer questions
-- the golden question set contains 30 questions about language models
-- python checks which expected keywords appear in each answer
-- the program saves answers, scores, and statuses to a csv file
-- a score of 60% or higher is marked pass; lower scores are marked review

-- what i did

I ran the first 30-question evaluation and recorded it as Release v0.1. The run had 12 pass, 17 review, and 1 error (Q007), with 48.89% average keyword coverage.

Files: main.py, golden_set.json, requirements.txt, baseline_results.csv
